      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $w(x)={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={e}^{2x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(x) & =({e}^{2x})^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+{e}^{2x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x)^{′} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+{e}^{2x}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
